        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "307bcc7f-cef8-5dc0-a79a-0adc01e91138",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game\n- Places: BB&T Center, Sunrise, Florida, Winter Haven, Florida\n- Organizations: Florida Panthers, Florida House of Representatives\n- People: Baxter Troutman\n- Topics: 2002–03 NHL season, 2002–03 Florida Panthers season\n\nFacts:\n- The BB&T Center in Sunrise, Florida, was completed in 1998 at a cost of US$185 million, was almost entirely publicly financed, and features 70 suites and 2,623 club seats.\n- The BB&T Center in Sunrise, Florida, was previously known as the National Car Rental Center, Office Depot Center, and BankAtlantic Center.\n- The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game was held on February 2, 2003, during the 2002–03 NHL season at the Office Depot Center in Sunrise, Florida, which was the home arena of the Florida Panthers.\n- During the 2002–03 Florida Panthers season, the Florida Panthers did not make the playoffs but hosted the 53rd All-Star Game.\n- Baxter Troutman is a citrus grower, businessman, and Republican politician from Winter Haven, Florida, who served as the representative for District 66 in the Florida House of Representatives.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "610c8fb2-775e-5605-94a3-9833b41807e1",
        "text": "Page: 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game. Sentence: The 53rd National Hockey League All-Star Game was held during the 2002–03 NHL season, and took place at the Office Depot Center in Sunrise, Florida, the home of the Florida Panthers, on February 2, 2003.\nPage: BB&amp;T Center (Sunrise, Florida). Sentence: The BB&T Center (previously known as the National Car Rental Center, Office Depot Center, and BankAtlantic Center) is an indoor arena located in Sunrise, Florida.\nPage: BB&amp;T Center (Sunrise, Florida). Sentence: It was completed in 1998, at a cost of US$185 million, almost entirely publicly financed, and features 70 suites and 2,623 club seats.\nPage: 2002–03 Florida Panthers season. Sentence: They didn't make the playoffs, but did host the 53rd All-Star Game that season.\nPage: Baxter Troutman. Sentence: Baxter Troutman is a Winter Haven, Florida Citrus Grower, businessman, and Republican politician who served as the representative for District 66 in the House of Representatives of the U.S. state of Florida.",
